  "id": "mixed-design",
  "term": "mixed design",
  "definition": "A mixed design is a research design used to study the combined effects of different factors in one study. In this packet, it refers to examining translation performance by relating learners’ anxiety levels to how the same learners perform on translation tasks with different complexity levels.",
